# A program in C's compact model (roadmap memory.md M5;
# tests/programs/tables.c): the pointers in its initialised data, which
# tools/mkexe makes selectors from wlink's relocations, read right; the far
# libraries on its data and its stack.
program: tables
match: contains
timeout: 30
---
tables: names: alpha beta gamma
tables: primes 2 3 5 7 11; squares 1 4 9
tables: the greeting: hello; through a pointer to .bss: 3
tables: their selector the data's: yes
tables: memcpy, memmove, memset and memcmp: yes
tables: rx_kcall and rx_xchg on the stack: yes
tables: the kernel's log from the stack
tables: done
